============================================================
                 DELTA LAN MESSENGER 2.0
============================================================

       Private Communication. Local Control.
                  Your Network.

Delta LAN Messenger is a self-hosted, Discord-inspired
communication platform designed for Local Area Networks.

It allows users connected to the same private network to
communicate through a web browser without requiring public
internet services during normal operation.

The application uses a central Ubuntu server and supports
real-time messaging, multiple servers, text channels,
administrative roles, file sharing, folder sharing and
browser-based voice communication.

============================================================
1. FEATURES
============================================================

MESSAGING
- Real-time text messaging.
- Multiple servers.
- Multiple text channels.
- Persistent message history.
- Online member presence.

SERVER MANAGEMENT
- Create and join servers.
- Discover available servers.
- Switch and leave servers.
- Server settings.
- Member management.

ROLES AND PERMISSIONS
- Server Owner.
- Administrator.
- Member.
- Channel creation and management.
- Channel access restrictions.

FILE SHARING
- Individual file sharing.
- Multiple file uploads.
- Complete folder sharing.
- Folder structure preservation.
- Upload progress.
- ZIP folder downloads.

VOICE COMMUNICATION
- Real-time browser voice chat.
- WebRTC peer-to-peer audio.
- Microphone mute controls.
- Join and leave voice channels.

