============================================================
4. INSTALLATION ON UBUNTU
============================================================

STEP 1: UPDATE THE SYSTEM

sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y

STEP 2: INSTALL REQUIRED PACKAGES

sudo apt install -y nodejs npm openssl unzip dos2unix

STEP 3: CHECK NODE.JS

node --version
npm --version

Ensure Node.js is version 18 or newer.

STEP 4: EXTRACT THE PROJECT

Extract the downloaded project ZIP file.

Navigate into the extracted project directory:

cd /path/to/delta-lan-messenger-v2

Replace the example path with your actual project location.

STEP 5: SET FILE PERMISSIONS

sudo chown -R "$USER":"$USER" .

STEP 6: FIX SCRIPT LINE ENDINGS

dos2unix scripts/*.sh

STEP 7: MAKE INSTALLATION SCRIPTS EXECUTABLE

chmod +x scripts/*.sh

STEP 8: INSTALL THE APPLICATION

./scripts/install-ubuntu.sh

The installation script prepares dependencies, environment
configuration and HTTPS certificates.

STEP 9: START THE APPLICATION

npm start

Your Delta LAN Messenger server should now be running.

============================================================
5. ACCESS THE APPLICATION
============================================================

After starting the server, access it through a browser.

Use the server's local network address:

https://SERVER-LAN-IP:5000

Replace SERVER-LAN-IP with the actual LAN IP address
of the Ubuntu server.

For local testing on the Ubuntu computer:

https://localhost:5000

The HTTPS certificate must be trusted by client browsers
for reliable microphone access.

============================================================
6. FIND YOUR SERVER IP ADDRESS
============================================================

To find the Ubuntu server's local IP address:

hostname -I

Or:

ip addr

Use the appropriate LAN address when connecting other
computers.

============================================================
7. COMMON SERVER COMMANDS
============================================================

START SERVER:

npm start

INSTALL DEPENDENCIES:

npm install

RUN TESTS:

npm test

CHECK PORT 5000:

sudo lsof -i :5000

CHECK SERVER HEALTH:

curl -k https://localhost:5000/health

STOP SERVER:

Press CTRL + C in the terminal running the application.

RESTART SERVER:

Stop the existing process using CTRL + C,
then execute:

npm start

IMPORTANT:
Do not start another server instance if port 5000
is already occupied by your running application.

============================================================
8. WINDOWS CLIENT SETUP
============================================================

1. Connect to the same private network as the server.
2. Open Chrome, Edge or another supported browser.
3. Trust the server's HTTPS certificate.
4. Visit the server's LAN address.
5. Choose a display name.
6. Join a server.
7. Start messaging and sharing files.

Allow microphone permission to use voice channels.

============================================================
9. AUTOMATIC SERVER STARTUP
============================================================

The project includes a systemd service configuration.

The service can be enabled to start automatically
when Ubuntu boots.

Enable and start:

sudo systemctl enable --now delta-lan-messenger

Check status:

sudo systemctl status delta-lan-messenger

View logs:

sudo journalctl -u delta-lan-messenger -f

============================================================
10. DATA STORAGE AND BACKUPS
============================================================

The application stores its data locally.

data/
  store.json
  uploads/

store.json:
Contains server, channel, membership, message and
file metadata.

uploads/:
Contains uploaded files.

Back up both locations together.

Stop the application before performing a backup.

============================================================
11. TROUBLESHOOTING
============================================================

ERROR: CANNOT FIND MODULE 'EXPRESS'

Solution:

npm install

ERROR: BASH\\r NOT FOUND

Solution:

dos2unix scripts/*.sh
chmod +x scripts/*.sh

ERROR: INSTALLATION SCRIPT NOT FOUND

Check the correct directory:

ls scripts/

Run:

./scripts/install-ubuntu.sh

ERROR: ADDRESS ALREADY IN USE

Solution:

sudo lsof -i :5000

Check whether another instance of the application
is already running.

Do not kill an unknown process.

ERROR: WEBSITE CANNOT CONNECT

Check:

sudo lsof -i :5000

Check server health:

curl -k https://localhost:5000/health

Also check the server IP address and firewall settings.

============================================================
12. SECURITY INFORMATION
============================================================

Delta LAN Messenger is designed for trusted private
networks.

Current limitations:

- No authenticated account system.
- Display names can be impersonated.
- No end-to-end encryption.
- The server can read stored messages and files.
- Channel permissions are not a security boundary
  against malicious LAN users.

Do not expose the application directly to the public
internet without implementing appropriate security.

============================================================
13. PROJECT GOAL
============================================================

Delta LAN Messenger aims to provide a private,
self-hosted alternative to traditional communication
platforms.

It gives users control over their own messaging server,
communication channels, file storage and voice system.

